Version: 1.0
desc: calfNXT Aligner
tags: processing alignment delay phase multi-mic mixer
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  An eight lane time aligner and mixer for multi-microphone recordings. Each lane has a delay trim (relative to the
  lane it is joined to when Join is on), polarity flip, gain, pan, mute and solo. The lane delays are made non-negative by
  padding every lane, and the pad is reported to the host as plugin delay compensation. Master delay trims the whole mix:
  positive values delay the audio, negative values are reported as delay compensation instead. A stereo Reference input
  (channels 9 and 10) shows a reference waveform. An analysis band-pass (12 to 48 dB/oct high and low pass) feeds the hit
  waveforms and the per lane correlation meters.
  Inputs: channels 1 to 8 are the lanes, 9 and 10 the stereo reference. Output: stereo mix.
  Ported from the Aligner in calfNXT by Markus Schmidt (https://calfnxt.org), GNU GPL 3.
  JSFX version released under GPLv3 license
  Claude generated some of this code

